  "configuration_id": "config_038",
  "reason": "The two completed experiments show image-only (resnet50, singleprofile) is very weak (acc 0.208) while multimodal with scgpt+resnet50 and weighted fusion jumps to 0.421. This large gap tells us RNA information is critical, but it does not decompose how much of the 0.421 comes from the RNA modality alone versus the image modality or their interaction. Config_038 (rna_only, singleprofile, scgpt) is the cleanest next experiment: it removes the image branch from config_009 while keeping the same RNA encoder and profile setting, isolating the marginal contribution of the image modality. If RNA alone approaches ~0.40, the image adds little and future budget should target RNA encoder or profile improvements; if RNA alone is substantially lower (e.g., ~0.25–0.30), the multimodal fusion is genuinely valuable and we should next optimize fusion strategy and image encoder. Resolving this uncertainty before testing fusion variants (config_012) or image encoder upgrades (config_002) ensures we invest the remaining budget on the modality that actually drives performance, making this the highest-information experiment under the limited budget."
}

